Description: Check for a resource before printing it when a commit is retried.
 An extractor may succeed without finding any metadata, which leaves the extract info without
 a resource. When committing such an item failed, for example because the file vanished and
 was removed from the database in the meantime, retry_synchronously() passed the NULL resource
 to tracker_resource_print_sparql_update(). tinysparql returns a static empty string on that
 precondition failure, and freeing it aborted the extractor with "free(): invalid pointer".
 .
 The SPARQL is printed only when there is a resource, as tracker_decorator_update() already
 does.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/localsearch/-/merge_requests/707
Last-Update: 2026-11-01
--- a/src/extractor/tracker-decorator.c
+++ b/src/extractor/tracker-decorator.c
@@ -397,15 +397,18 @@ retry_synchronously (TrackerDecorator *d
 			GFile *file;
 
 			/* This is a SPARQL/ontology error, set the SPARQL query
-			 * as the the extra information.
+			 * as the extra information. There is none when the
+			 * extractor found no metadata.
 			 */
 			file = tracker_extract_info_get_file (info);
 			graph = tracker_extract_info_get_graph (info);
 			resource = tracker_extract_info_get_resource (info);
 
-			sparql = tracker_resource_print_sparql_update (resource,
-			                                               NULL,
-			                                               graph);
+			if (resource) {
+				sparql = tracker_resource_print_sparql_update (resource,
+				                                               NULL,
+				                                               graph);
+			}
 
 			tracker_decorator_raise_error (decorator, file,
 			                               error->message, sparql);
